Replay determinism hooks for a test harness. PS2Memory::saveDeterministicTimer0 / restoreDeterministicTimer0 read and set the state of patch 0154's deterministic timer 0 (on, the count's writes, the reads since the last write), so every replayed run can start from the same state and a call that reads the count as a random number reads the same values in each run. EeScheduler::cycleCount gives the EE cycles counted so far, so a harness that stands in for the wait for the vertical blank can move time (and with it the IOP, which runs on those cycles) on to the same point in every run, as the wait does.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_memory.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_memory.h
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_memory.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_memory.h
@@ -336,6 +336,16 @@ public:
